# A founding-file principle with a present-but-blank '## Rule' is a hard error
# (exit 2), not a silently-dropped catalog-only record: rule input is
# validated, never silently swallowed. The message names the offending
# principle. Nothing is seeded. Locks the contract (implementation-plan §8).

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-02

exitcode 2 constitution init --founding-file principles.md --founding-category architecture --category architecture
stderr 'principle "Tests are mandatory" has a "## Rule" section that is present but empty; give it a rule statement or remove the heading \(a catalog-only principle has no "## Rule"\)'

# no founding ADR was seeded
! exists constitution/adr/ADR-0001-tests-are-mandatory.md

-- principles.md --
## Tests are mandatory

Every change ships with tests.

## Rule

